  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltspangtThis locally led
project addresses urgent EiE, Food Security, and&#xa0;Protection/MRE/GBV,&#xa0;needs of IDP and vulnerable groups in7 townships of Taungoo, Phyu, Thandaunggyi, Shwegyin, Nyaunglebin, Thaton and Bilin&#xa0;of Kayin, Mon and Bago.
Implementation will take place in 60 IDP camps/clusters and host communities
with multi-sector interventions targeting areas of greatest need, reaching a
total of 24,620 Individuals&#xa0; &#xa0; &#xa0; (5,832 men, 8,156 women, 4,699 boys, 5,933 girls) including 3,446 people
with disabilities (PWDs). The target areas are affected by the
ongoing conflict in Kayin, Mon and East Bago with the
majority of the population displaced and living in makeshift IDP camps in the
forest, host communities. This project aims to contribute to the reduction of
the immediate suffering of IDP in these target areas by providing rapid
multi-sectoral support, in coordination with other actors working in SE regions and in alignment with the priorities of this allocation.ltbrgtltbrgt
A conflict-sensitive approach will be followed towards the inclusion of
vulnerable people in all project sites. Specific vulnerable groups such as
PWDs, PSNs and female headed households will be prioritized according to
cluster/sector guidelines. The project will consider women&#x2019;s specific needs.
Gender balanced staff will be recruited where possible, women will be
separately engaged in consultations/training and gender dis aggregated data will
be collected. AAP, inclusion and protection, prevention of GBV/SEA,
environmental risks, localization and social cohesion will be mainstreamed
throughout.lt/spangt ltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtKMSS, ECNKR (Environmental Conservation Natural Resources Management in Kayan Region) have pre-existing and are well positioned to implement this
project due to their combined sectoral experience and longstanding presence in
the target locations. KMSS is currently implementing humanitarian and
development programs in Kayin, Mon and Bago region with KMSS staff based in the
communities. ltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtTo continued this project implementation on the ground, KMSS will work with local based CSOs and volunteer groups working in EAO Controlled Areas of Kayin and Bago Regions. Name of KMSS partners to work with KMSS for this project under EAO Controlled Areas are not mentioned in the proposal document because of  their request and sensitivity due to ongoing conflict in the regions. ltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtKMSS will seek the technical support from CRS (Catholic Relief Services) for CBI as CRS is long term partner in Myanmar. ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
